WEBVTT

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.980
The fact that not everything in the world

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.400
can be explained with mathematics or physics.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.490
Huh?

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.530
My ideas originate in my dreams.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.040
And through experimentation with mathematics and physics,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.240
I prove them.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.090
Let's go!

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.250
Okay!

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.320
Fly!

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.150
It'll fly this time!

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.700
What about now?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.400
Catch the wind!

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.250
The cloud you saw when you arrived

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.300
has appeared many times before.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.210
I think it extremely likely that it shall come again.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:22.010
We have to time the flight with its appearance, so I can reach the cloud.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.690
I have to return...

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.170
You seem desperate.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.290
We've isolated most of the issues.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.160
Yeah.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.690
We'll fix them as soon as we get back.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.160
Look, Hozuki!

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.870
It's the cloud.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:56.950
The Tesoro is doing it again...

00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.530
Here it comes.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:22.580
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:22.580
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:30.370
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:30.370
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:37.630
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:37.630
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.720
shinkuromanika

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.720
Synchromanica

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.260
itsu no ma ni ka

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.260
Before I know it

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.430
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.430
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:50.730
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:50.730
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:57.230
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:57.230
I can hear someone's dream

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:04.200
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:04.200
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.000
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.000
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.340
shinkuromanika

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.340
Synchromanica

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.470
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.470
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.510
shinkuromanika

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.510
Synchromanica

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.730
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.730
The synchrony of your life

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.440
Space-Time Goldfish
(Part 2)

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.110
1, 2, 3...

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.370
4, 5, 6...

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.370
Extrapolating from past data,

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.870
it'll happen again early tomorrow evening.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.160
Tomorrow evening...

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:01.050
There's still time.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.380
Let's correct those issues immediately.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.080
Okay.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.250
I think we'll be all right now!

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.630
It would be best if we could do a test flight first, but...

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.680
Don't worry.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.090
It'll definitely work.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.220
What are you doing?

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.640
I'm tracking the motion of the stars and the Moon.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.650
That telescope... Did you make it yourself?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.280
Amazing, isn't it?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.400
I bought the lens from a Dutch spectacle-maker.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.570
Is this...

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.870
a sketch of the Moon?

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.730
Yeah. Realistic, isn't it?

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.080
This is...

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.170
When you look at the Moon through this,

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:03.050
you can see that the boundary between the bright and dark areas isn't smooth.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.400
The Moon isn't a perfect sphere.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:12.180
Many philosophers and astronomers believe

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.850
that all stars in the sky orbit the Earth.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.150
They believe that the Earth lies at the center of the universe, but...

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:25.490
I've come to doubt what everyone has believed until now.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.680
Or rather, I have come to realize that they're mistaken.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.370
Because of that, I'd like to show
everyone the truth someday, but...

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.160
Yeah...

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.810
But because I'm a nobody, nobody would listen to my theory of heliocentrism.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:47.420
When faced with a reality that they have never experienced before,

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.850
most people will reject it.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.100
They will refuse to accept it

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.650
and try to discredit it any way that they can.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:02.100
People fear new truths...

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.320
But I do not.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.860
I doubt the conventional truths. I'm compelled to observe,

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.530
experiment and prove their veracity.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.010
That's what real physicists do.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:18.790
Hozuki, I'd like to ask you something.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.330
Huh?

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:25.340
Observation of you has led me to a certain conclusion...

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.440
Although I still struggle to comprehend it.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.250
You are not from this time, are you?

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:38.710
No.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.150
A severe fuel shortage?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.360
Yeah.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.380
So that's what will happen to Earth...

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:54.360
I was traveling with Haa-nee, Kaa-nee and Anna-san.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:57.080
Then, did you find a solution?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:01.870
Just as we were about to, I was sent to this time period.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:05.720
I cannot see how such a thing is possible

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:08.550
from a theoretical, scientific perspective...

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.860
But reality disagrees.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:13.350
A lot of things happened.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:19.770
It was tough, sad and fun... All of those.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.270
But right as everything was coming to a head, this happened.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.770
Don't be so discouraged...

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.190
You'll see your family again.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.280
I'm sure of it.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.390
Yes.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.580
Japanese candy!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.890
You know these?

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:49.270
Yeah, I love them!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.560
I didn't know they'd been around so long.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.530
Delicious!

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.720
Although, they could be a little sweeter...

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.600
I often eat them when I feel stuck.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.900
I eat them all the time!

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.610
To think that this candy will exist so far in the future...

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.320
Sweet things energize the brain.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.490
Really?

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.300
All right!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.890
I'll eat them often and study a lot!

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.170
Nothing's showing up...

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:55.470
I wonder who that love letter was written to...

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.450
And when...

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.540
This is...

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:10.040
This is still new!

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.720
It won't be long now.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.080
Yeah.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.690
Don't worry.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.210
If we follow the calculations,

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.330
it should be fine.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.220
What's this?

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.970
It's called a goldfish.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:03.930
A goldfish?

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.140
Picco Rosso.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.240
It's traveled with me this whole time.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.520
Then it's something precious to you?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.630
Yeah!

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:14.980
It's a gift.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.870
Are you sure?

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.570
But isn't it important to you?

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.000
To thank you!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:21.820
Thank me?

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.370
For letting me spend time with you.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.330
It was really fun and super interesting.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.090
So I'm thanking you for that.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.080
I'd like you to have it.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.460
Very well.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.120
I'll hang onto it, then.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.890
Thank you, Hozuki.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.970
I'll take good care of it.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:53.010
But actually, it's I who should be thanking you.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:53.830
Huh?

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.440
You helped me, didn't you?

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.070
Okay, let's go.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.080
Right!

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.440
We did it!

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.900
It's flying?

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.780
It's flying!

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:49.950
We managed to fly.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.370
We're flying...

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.250
It's in stable flight!

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.260
Yeah.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.430
The horizon's curved!

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.530
Yeah.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.810
When I was a child,

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.850
I used to look out at the ocean

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.330
and wonder if the Earth was round!

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:23.490
Although all of the mathematical formulas and astronomical observations theorize

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:27.860
that the Earth is round and rotates on its axis,
I couldn't be sure without seeing it!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.610
Now I know that the Earth is round...

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:35.500
That has been proven.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.330
I'm happy for you.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.880
I shall no longer waver.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.590
It's thanks to you, Hozuki.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:48.720
Huh?

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.890
I can be confident in following my own path.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.390
What do you mean?

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:58.020
I've always wanted to soar through the sky

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.900
and see things through my own eyes.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.690
But whenever I spoke of that dream,

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.820
everybody looked at me as if I were insane...

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.410
They thought me a madman,

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.330
imagining the impossible.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:19.620
And people began to distance
themselves from me because of it.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.210
I didn't want to be looked at that way,

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:26.250
so I stopped telling people about my dreams.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:32.550
Eventually, I even ceased trying to make others understand me.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:42.880
"Until now, I had never felt any need to be understood.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.570
I had never felt lonely...

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:49.320
Not until I met you."

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:55.450
I did hold on to my desire to fly and to see things for myself.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:15:00.150
And now, thanks to you, I've been able to prove something!

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.750
So I won't waver anymore.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:08.180
I've been able to reaffirm my resolve

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:10.570
to follow the path that I believe in.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.800
Thank you, Hozuki.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:21.740
Galileo...

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:22.310
Hmm?

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:25.110
I feel that way, as well.

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:25.910
Oh?

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:30.320
I was always alone, too.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:35.320
I could never really tell anyone around me what I was thinking.

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:40.320
Actually, it was more like I couldn't explain my thoughts to them...

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.450
So I think I understand how you feel.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:53.340
But I'm no longer alone.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:57.680
Besides, during my journey, I've come to realize

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.690
that there's something I have to do.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.440
I'm sure you'll also

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.700
find someone who understands you.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.570
I've already found them!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.780
Huh?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:21.080
Not only did you understand me, you helped refine my thoughts.

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:24.960
Hozuki, you are that person.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.530
I'm no longer alone, either...

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.930
Moving forward, I can see things through.

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:40.180
When you return, do what you must.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.020
Right.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:48.480
Just now, I had a thought that was rather unlike me to have.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.170
Huh? What?

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.830
Well...

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:59.280
If only this could continue...

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:05.710
If only I could keep flying on the <i>Galileo</i> this way forever...

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.530
Flying beside you.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.300
Huh?

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:15.510
That's the thought that just sprang forth in my mind.

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:19.680
Galileo...

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:23.430
I feel the same way.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:32.940
Right, let's go!

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:33.690
Yes.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:51.830
"That summer, due to your sudden appearance...

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:56.500
I learned about an emotion unique to humanity.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.840
That terribly ambiguous, abstract notion

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.470
known as love, which is subject to neither proof nor verification.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.290
The Moon, floating in the night sky,

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:09.500
was a mere object for observation 'til now.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:14.480
But I shall never forget the Moon I saw with you, on that summer night.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.070
I shall never forget, not for the rest of my life."

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:29.000
"Faced with the reality that I shall never see you again,

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:35.510
I learned for the first time how difficult and painful farewells can be.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.510
When I touched you,

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.630
I reached a decision...

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:46.190
That I would surely make your wish come true myself."

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.530
We're nearly there!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:07.500
Galileo, um...

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:08.580
Hozuki!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.880
Galileo!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.000
Hozuki, I...

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:27.250
Hozuki!

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.100
Galileo!

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.370
Go, Bambina!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.400
I'll protect you!

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.640
BlaGany...

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.530
Kakkii, Hocchii, let's make a run for it!

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.650
Hocchibi, full speed ahead!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.050
<i>Galileo</i>, taking flight!

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:29.990
Launch!

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.270
Galileo...

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:05.030
All systems down on the <i>Galileo</i>.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:05.570
This is the Interpol.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:09.250
Good night, Hozuki-chan...

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:09.130
Surrender without resistance, Ferrari sisters.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:12.030
You are completely surrounded.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.040
We repeat:

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:16.040
Resistance is futile, Ferrari sisters.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.150
Surrender without resistance.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:41.020
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:41.020
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:44.860
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:44.860
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:51.870
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:51.870
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:57.000
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:57.000
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.380
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.380
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:06.670
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:06.670
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:14.640
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:14.640
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:23.020
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:23.020
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:30.160
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:30.160
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:42.290
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:42.290
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
